  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the given figure, a battery of emf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> is connected across a conductor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>&nbsp;and different area&nbsp;of cross-sections having radii <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0180_ffe33e9e96a8.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 188px;\" /></p><p>Choose the correct option as one moves from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>.</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Drift velocity of electron increases.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Electric field decreases.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Electron current decreases.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "All of these",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0180_f1ea28ff0537.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 93px;\" /></p><p>Current is constant in conductor<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo></math>constant<br />Resistance of element <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>&#160;ipdx&#160;</mtext><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>&#961;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br />and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>&#964;</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>E</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> decreases, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> will increase.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></math> will increase.</p>"
  }
